      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{60651324fbe2815d2b9ff6cb|full_name} 95% of responders want a label, I'm one of them.  100% of those 95% couldn't agree on what that label means, there was a pretty sizable spectrum of thought there.  So what's the solution?  Do we go with the meaning that Sky wants to go with?  What about the meaning that KiwiPoku wanted to go with?  Suppose one is more strict than the other?  If VRChat goes with one, will the other still be angry and still harass VRChat every time they post something?\n\nOr is the solution to implement a whole spectrum of AI tags (I guess 3000 some variants?), which becomes meaningless almost immediately.\n\nAnd how is it enforced?  Who makes up the Spanish Inquisition here?  Who holds them accountable?\n\nLet's actually figure out a plan, instead of just going off by feelings here.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
